  ▌ sshpick pick [query]...

  Pick a host from ~/.ssh/config and ssh to it. Exactly one match connects at
  once, without opening the picker.

  Keys:
  Enter                        ssh to the selected host
  Esc, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-G, Ctrl-Q  quit (exit 130); Esc closes this help first
  Up, Ctrl-P, Ctrl-K           select the previous host; wraps to the last
  Down, Ctrl-N, Ctrl-J         select the next host; wraps to the first
  type                         filter; 'exact ^prefix suffix$ !not
  Backspace, Ctrl-H            delete the last character
  Ctrl-U                       clear the filter
  Ctrl-W                       delete the last word
  Ctrl-D                       quit when the filter is empty
  ?, F1                        toggle this help (? only on an empty filter)

  Global Options: See `sshpick --help`

  Examples:
  Open the picker filtered to hosts matching both words
    sshpick new consul

  Connect to one host by its exact name, and never open the picker
    sshpick --non-interactive stg-bastion

  Search for a word that is also a command name
    sshpick pick list
